<ansi fg="black-bold">.:</ansi> <ansi fg="magenta">Help for </ansi><ansi fg="command">harvest</ansi>

See what a carcass can still give, or take one part with extra care.

  <ansi fg="command">harvest <corpse></ansi>               list what is left and which tool each needs
  <ansi fg="command">harvest <part> from <corpse></ansi>   take just that part
  <ansi fg="command">harvest <corpse> <part></ansi>        the same

Taking a single part is a harder job than skinning or butchering the whole
carcass, but done well it comes out one grade better. Use it for the part
that matters: the pelt of a prize animal, an antler, a gland.

<ansi fg="yellow">See Also:</ansi>

  <ansi fg="command">help skin</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help butcher</ansi>, <ansi fg="command">help tools</ansi>
